{"ts": "2026-10-26T03:12:07.508226Z", "run_id": "r-20261026T0311Z-4b41", "unit": "openspec:vault-method-scopes", "seq": 16, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "The question is the design's own \"none that block\" note, lifted verbatim from its Open questions section. The proposal (Impact, out-of-scope list) explicitly excludes tenant checks on the caller from this unit, and the design repeats that it is a separate concern. The spec's requirements and scenarios only cover method scopes, open health methods, stream refusal and boot-identity scopes. The unit's documents therefore settle it: no decision is needed, and no task depends on a tenant check.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1", "2.1"], "target": null, "kind": "ambiguous", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.9251562499999999, "decision": "answer", "answer_sha256": "f909740e5e3be45a1ab57a35775ca2dfbc135c6d1803ca086d97d6ddbee80bd4", "checked": [{"ref": "spec:proposal.md#impact", "quote": "Out of scope: tenant checks on the caller (an identity with `vault.read` still reads any tenant's credential)", "claim": "The proposal explicitly excludes the tenant check on the caller from this change."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md#open-questions", "quote": "None that block. The tenant check on the caller (an identity reads every tenant's credentials) is a separate concern.", "claim": "The design states that no open question blocks the unit and that the tenant check is a separate concern."}, {"ref": "spec:tasks.md#2-each-boot-identity-holds-only-the-scopes-it-uses", "quote": "set the proxy entry's `Scopes` to\n  `[]string{\"vault.read\"}` and the SSH proxy entry's to `[]string{\"vault.read\", \"vault.hostkey.put\"}`; nothing else in\n  the file changes.", "claim": "The tasks define the scope of 1.1 and 2.1 without any tenant check on the caller."}]}
